Interview-Level Understanding

If an interviewer asks:

"Explain Terraform architecture."

A strong answer is:

Terraform consists of Terraform Core and Provider Plugins. Terraform Core reads .tf configuration files, creates a dependency graph, compares the desired state with the current state stored in terraform.tfstate,
generates an execution plan, and then communicates with cloud providers through provider plugins.
The provider plugin translates Terraform requests into cloud API calls (AWS, Azure, GCP).
After resources are created or modified, Terraform updates the state file so it can track infrastructure changes in future runs.
